sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant API as create-order Lambda
    participant DB as DynamoDB (Orders)
    participant EB as EventBridge
    participant SFN as Step Functions
    participant INV as inventory Lambda
    participant PAY as payment Lambda
    participant FRAUD as fraud Lambda
    participant SQS as SQS queues
    participant SHIP as shipping Lambda
    participant NOTIFY as notification Lambda

    C->>API: POST /orders (idempotency-key, correlation-id)
    API->>DB: create order (status=RECEIVED)
    API->>EB: publish OrderCreated
    API-->>C: 202 { orderId, status: RECEIVED }

    Note over EB,SFN: rule "order-created" starts the workflow
    EB->>SFN: start execution

    SFN->>INV: CheckInventory task
    INV->>DB: update status (PROCESSING | OUT_OF_STOCK)
    INV->>EB: publish InventoryValidated | InventoryFailed

    alt inventory available
        SFN->>PAY: ProcessPayment task
        PAY->>DB: update status (PROCESSING | PAYMENT_FAILED)
        PAY->>EB: publish PaymentApproved | PaymentFailed

        alt payment approved
            SFN->>FRAUD: CheckFraud task
            FRAUD->>DB: update status (APPROVED | FRAUD_DETECTED)
            FRAUD->>EB: publish FraudApproved | FraudRejected

            alt fraud approved
                SFN->>EB: PublishOrderApproved task
                Note over EB,SQS: rule "order-approved" -> shipping-queue
                EB->>SQS: route to shipping-queue
                SQS->>SHIP: deliver message
                SHIP->>DB: update status (SHIPPING then DELIVERED)
                SHIP->>EB: publish ShippingStarted, ShippingCompleted
            else fraud rejected
                Note over EB,SQS: rule "fraud-rejected" -> notification-queue
                EB->>SQS: route to notification-queue
                SQS->>NOTIFY: deliver message
                NOTIFY-->>NOTIFY: log notification (email/sms/push)
            end
        else payment failed
            Note over EB,SQS: rule "payment-failed" -> notification-queue
            EB->>SQS: route to notification-queue
            SQS->>NOTIFY: deliver message
            NOTIFY-->>NOTIFY: log notification
        end
    else out of stock
        Note over EB,SQS: rule "inventory-failed" -> notification-queue
        EB->>SQS: route to notification-queue
        SQS->>NOTIFY: deliver message
        NOTIFY-->>NOTIFY: log notification
    end

    Note over SQS: unprocessable messages land on the dead-letter queue after max receives

    C->>API: GET /orders/{id} (poll)
    API->>DB: read order
    API-->>C: 200 { status }
